ac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-22T20:32:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the candidates and what are the priorities after TCU fired Sonny Dykes?","description":"Things started well for Dykes, but now the Horned Frogs are looking for a new coach and should have options.","published":"2026-11-22T19:55:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50323301/tcu-candidates-personnel-recruits","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman, Max Olson and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-22T19:15:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5136784/francis-brewu","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Francis Brewu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Brewu","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:30Z","intro":"Francis Brewu (born January 17, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In January 2024, Brewu enrolled early at Pittsburgh. He quickly impressed during spring camp due to his size and technique and was moved off of the scout team. He was also named the strongest player on the team by his teammates. Prior to the 2024 season, Brewu was named number 77 on Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List. During the season he played in 12 games with one start and totaled 15 tackles, three tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. He was also named to the Pro Football Focus (PFF) All-Freshman Team at the end of the season. In December 2024, Brewu announced he would return to the Panthers for 2025. On August 4, 2025, Brewu was again named to Feldman's Freaks List, this time at number 24. In 2025 Brewu started 12 games for the Panthers in which he led all Pitt interior defensive linemen in tackles. Due to his performance, Brewu gained recognition as an Honorable Mention All-ACC selection. On January 6, 2026, Brewu entered the transfer portal, and chose to transfer to the Notre Dame Fighting Irish on January 13. On August 10, 2026, Brewu was named to Bruce Feldman’s Freaks List for the third consecutive season."}]}}